cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use GDS-ParT-MoE in research or a report, please cite it as below."
title: "GDS-ParT-MoE: per-particle Mixture-of-Experts for physics interpretability of the Gated Dual-Stream Particle Transformer"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Avinash
    alias: Avinashistoocool
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-30
repository-code: "https://github.com/Avinashistoocool/GDS-parT-MoE"
url: "https://avinashistoocool.github.io/GDS-parT-MoE/"
abstract: >-
  GDS-ParT-MoE adds a per-particle Mixture-of-Experts to the Gated Dual-Stream Particle Transformer (GDS-ParT)
  for jet tagging on JetClass. In every transformer block the particle feed-forward network is replaced by a
  router and 8 expert FFNs; each real jet constituent is routed to its top-2 experts with renormalised weights,
  trained with a Switch load-balancing loss and a router z-loss. The model is built by sparse upcycling from a
  trained dense GDS-ParT checkpoint, so the untrained MoE reproduces the dense model exactly. An analysis
  toolkit relates routing decisions to particle physics (species, charge, momentum share, angle to the jet axis,
  impact parameter, Lund-plane kT) through routing statistics, normalised mutual information and expert
  knockout. In a first, preliminary run (one epoch on 300k jets) the upcycled model keeps 84.7% validation
  accuracy and its first-layer router partitions particles by charge and species, with one expert specialising
  in muons and displaced tracks.
keywords:
  - particle physics
  - jet tagging
  - JetClass
  - transformer
  - mixture of experts
  - sparse upcycling
  - interpretability
  - GDS-ParT
  - PyTorch
